# Cloudflare Setup

The application uses two stable Worker projects and branch-isolated D1 previews:

- production Worker: `@@APP_NAME@@`
- preview Worker: `@@PREVIEW_WORKER_NAME@@`
- production database: `@@APP_NAME@@-production`
- stable preview database: `@@APP_NAME@@-staging`
- branch database: `@@APP_NAME@@-preview-{sanitized-branch}`

List every other binding here and state whether branch previews isolate or share it.

## Workers Builds

Connect the repository to both Worker projects. Use `pnpm bundle` as the build command and `pnpm deploy:dynamic` as the deploy command. On the preview project, also replace the separate non-production branch deploy command with `pnpm deploy:dynamic`; its default Wrangler upload would bypass D1 provisioning.

- `@@APP_NAME@@`: set build variable `CLOUDFLARE_ENV=production`; build only the production branch.
- `@@PREVIEW_WORKER_NAME@@`: set build variable `CLOUDFLARE_ENV=preview`; build the production branch and non-production branches.

Verify the Workers Builds token for each project includes Account D1 Edit as well as Worker upload permissions. The dynamic deploy script lists, creates, migrates, and queries D1.

Preview URLs are public when enabled unless Cloudflare Access protects them. Document whether public access is intended and configure an Access policy when it is not.

The stable URLs belong in the `production` and `preview` vars in `wrangler.jsonc`. `DEPLOY_URL` and `PREVIEW_DEPLOY_URL` may override them.

## Stable Resources

Create stable D1 databases once:

```bash
pnpm wrangler d1 create @@APP_NAME@@-staging
pnpm wrangler d1 create @@APP_NAME@@-production
```

Document one-time creation of stable R2, KV, queues, or other resources here. Branch databases are created automatically.

## Deployment Lifecycle

- Production builds migrate and deploy `@@APP_NAME@@` against `@@APP_NAME@@-production`.
- The production branch on the preview project migrates and deploys `@@PREVIEW_WORKER_NAME@@` against `@@APP_NAME@@-staging`.
- Other preview builds create or reuse `@@APP_NAME@@-preview-{sanitized-branch}`, migrate it, patch the `@@D1_BINDING@@` binding, and upload an aliased Worker version.
- Every deploy records branch, build ID, commit SHA, and time in `deployment_history`.

## Runtime Secrets and Variables

Store non-secret variables in `wrangler.jsonc`. Configure Worker secrets separately for preview and production. Never put secret values in build variables intended only to choose an environment or in Wrangler `--var` arguments.

The deploy script sets these variables to the active stable or aliased URL:

```text
@@URL_VARS_SHELL_ARRAY@@
```

## Cleanup

When a pull request closes, `.github/workflows/cleanup-preview-db.yml` checks out trusted base-branch code and deletes the D1 database derived from the head branch.

Configure:

- GitHub repository variable `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID`
- GitHub repository secret `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` with Account D1 Edit, scoped to the target account

Manual cleanup:

```bash
pnpm cleanup:preview-db -- <branch-name>
```

Cleanup is idempotent and refuses to delete `main` or `master`. It does not delete shared bindings or Worker version history.
